A_036 - Personally, I also believe that in many cases, plastic could replace wood as a building material: it's mold and termite-resistant, comes in a variety of colors, and doesn't kill trees (and recycled plastics can also be used).
Of course, we need plastics that have the same workability characteristics as wood so they can be used with the same tools that already exist. Fortunately, these materials have already been invented.